Saved to `ADR-001-notification-architecture.md`.

The ADR evaluates Redis Streams vs. Kafka across throughput, ordering guarantees, message retention, consumer groups, exactly-once semantics, and operational complexity — then recommends Redis Streams given the constraints: no new infra, no Kafka experience, 2-week delivery window, and a 6-person team with no dedicated infra engineer. The exactly-once requirement for billing notifications is addressed with an idempotency-layer solution that both brokers require anyway at the consumer level.
